لمطورين","دعم لمستويات الخبرة المختلفة","ملاحظات فورية على الكود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["my-react-rules使用指南","React AI代理工具","Yihui编程练习","AI辅助React开发","my-react-rules安装","React学习工具","代码审查AI工具","my-react-rules替代方案","React vs Vue AI工具"],"ja":["my-react-rules使い方","React AIエージェント","Yihuiプログラミング練習","AI支援React開発","my-react-rulesインストール","React学習ツール","コードレビューAIツール","my-react-rules替代ツール","React vs Vue AIエージェント"],"ko":["my-react-rules 사용법","React AI 에이전트","Yihui 프로그래밍 실습","AI 지원 React 개발","my-react-rules 설치","React 학습 도구","코드 리뷰 AI 도구","my-react-rules 대체方案","React vs Vue AI 에이전트"],"es":["herramientas de IA para React","my-react-rules install","prácticas de programación React","herramientas de IA para desarrolladores","Yihui React follow up","my-react-rules setup guide","mejorar habilidades React","ejercicios React con IA"],"fr":["outils d''IA pour React","my-react-rules install","pratiques de programmation React","outils d''IA pour développeurs","Yihui React suivi","my-react-rules guide d''installation","améliorer les compétences React","exercices React avec IA"],"de":["KI-Tools für React","my-react-rules installieren","React-Programmierübungen","KI-Tools für Entwickler","Yihui React Follow-up","my-react-rules Setup-Anleitung","React-Fähigkeiten verbessern","React-Übungen mit KI"],"pt":["my-react-rules tutorial","ferramenta AI para React","prática programação React","como usar my-react-rules","exercícios React com IA","Yihui programação acompanhamento","my-react-rules vs código","instalar my-react-rules","setup my-react-rules guide","alternativa my-react-rules"],"ru":["my-react-rules руководство","ИИ инструмент для React","практика программирования React","как использовать my-react-rules","упражнения React с ИИ","Yihui программирование сопровождение","my-react-rules vs код","установить my-react-rules","настройка my-react-rules guide","альтернатива my-react-rules"],"ar":["برنامج تعليمي my-react-rules","أداة الذكاء الاصطناعي لـ React","ممارسة برمجة React","كيفية استخدام my-react-rules","تمارين React بالذكاء الاصطناعي","Yihui برمجة متابعة","my-react-rules مقابل كود","تثبيت my-react-rules","دليل إعداد my-react-rules","بديل my-react-rules"]}},"owner":"Aafff623","repo":"yihui-vibe-coding-exer","repoPath":"Aafff623/yihui-vibe-coding-exer","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-03T13:05:37.111Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"my-react-rules","description":"This is a new rule","bodyPreview":"# Overview\n\n# Elixir and Phoenix Best Practices\n\n_Based on Dave Thomas'' (PragDave) coding philosophy_\nImportant: always use lates versions of packages and libraries, including Phoenix.\n\n## Core Principles\n\n- **Domain-Driven Design**: Organize code around business domains, not technical layers\n- **Functional Core, Imperative Shell**: Pure domain logic with side effects at boundaries\n- **Explicit Over Implicit**: Prefer clarity over magic\n- **Composition Over Inheritance**: Build systems from smal","body":"# Overview\n\n# Elixir and Phoenix Best Practices\n\n_Based on Dave Thomas'' (PragDave) coding philosophy_\nImportant: always use lates versions of packages and libraries, including Phoenix.\n\n## Core Principles\n\n- **Domain-Driven Design**: Organize code around business domains, not technical layers\n- **Functional Core, Imperative Shell**: Pure domain logic with side effects at boundaries\n- **Explicit Over Implicit**: Prefer clarity over magic\n- **Composition Over Inheritance**: Build systems from small, focused components\n- **Single Responsibility**: Each module and function should do one thing well\n- **Easy to Change**: Design for maintainability and future change\n- **Fail Fast**: Detect and handle errors as early as possible\n- **YAGNI**: Don''t build features until they''re needed\n\n## Project Structure\n\n- **Context-Based Organization**: Use Phoenix contexts to define domain boundaries\n  lib/my_app/\n  accounts/ # User management domain\n  billing/ # Payment processing domain\n  catalog/ # Product catalog domain\n\n- **API/Implementation Separation**: Public API modules delegate to implementation modules\n\n  # In MyApp.Accounts (API module)\n\n  defdelegate create_user(attrs), to: MyApp.Accounts.UserCreator\n\n- **Boundary Enforcement**: Use tools like NimbleOptions to validate inputs at boundaries\n\n## Coding Patterns\n\n- **Pattern Matching**: Use pattern matching in function heads for control flow\n- **Railway-Oriented Programming**: Chain operations with ''with'' for elegant error handling\n\n  with {:ok, user} <- find_user(id),\n  {:ok, updated} <- update_user(user, attrs) do\n  {:ok, updated}\n  end\n\n- **Type Specifications**: Add typespecs to all public functions\n\n  @spec create_user(user_attrs()) :: {:ok, User.t()} | {:error, Changeset.t()}\n\n- **Immutable Data Transformations**: Return new state rather than modifying existing state\n\n- **Data Validation**: Validate data at boundaries using Ecto.Changeset even outside of database contexts\n\n  def validate_attrs(attrs) do\n  {%{}, %{name: :string, email: :string}}\n  |> Ecto.Changeset.cast(attrs, [:name, :email])\n  |> Ecto.Changeset.validate_required([:name, :email])\n  |> Ecto.Changeset.validate_format(:email, ~r/@/)\n  end\n\n- **Result Tuples**: Return tagged tuples like ''{:ok, result}'' or ''{:error, reason}'' for operations that can fail\n\n## Process Design\n\n- **GenServer for State**: Use GenServers for stateful processes\n- **Supervision Trees**: Design proper supervision hierarchies\n- **Registry Pattern**: Use Registry for dynamic process lookup\n- **Task.Supervisor**: Use for concurrent, potentially failing operations\n- **Process Isolation**: Design processes to crash independently without affecting the whole system\n- **Let It Crash**: Embrace the \"let it crash\" philosophy with proper supervision\n\n## Phoenix Best Practices\n\n- **LiveView-First**: Use LiveView as the primary UI technology\n- **Function Components**: Use function components for reusable UI elements\n- **PubSub for Real-time**: Use Phoenix PubSub for real-time features\n- **Context Boundaries**: Respect context boundaries in controllers and LiveViews\n- **Thin Controllers**: Keep controllers thin, delegating business logic to contexts\n- **Security First**: Always consider security implications (CSRF, XSS, etc.)\n\n## Testing Strategies\n\n- **Test Public APIs**: Focus on testing public context APIs\n- **Mox for Dependencies**: Use Mox for mocking external dependencies\n- **Property-Based Testing**: Use StreamData for property-based tests\n- **Test Factories**: Use ExMachina for test data creation\n- **Test Readability**: Write tests that serve as documentation\n- **Arrange-Act-Assert**: Structure tests with clear setup, action, and verification phases\n\n## HTTP and API Integration\n\n- **Req for HTTP Clients**: Use Req instead of HTTPoison or Tesla\n- **Behaviours for API Clients**: Define behaviours for API clients to allow easy mocking\n- **Error Handling**: Handle network failures and unexpected responses gracefully\n- **Timeouts**: Always set appropriate timeouts for external calls\n- **Circuit Breakers**: Use circuit breakers for critical external services\n\n## Naming Conventions\n\n- **Snake Case**: For variables and functions (''create_user'')\n- **Verb-First Functions**: Start function names with verbs (''create_user'', not ''user_create'')\n- **Plural for Collections**: Use plural for collections (''users'', not ''user'')\n- **Consistent Terminology**: Use consistent terms throughout the codebase\n- **Intention-Revealing Names**: Choose names that reveal intent, not implementation\n\n## Documentation and Quality\n\n- **Document Public Functions**: Add ''@doc'' to all public functions\n- **Examples in Docs**: Include examples in documentation\n- **Credo and Dialyzer**: Use for static analysis and type checking\n- **Consistent Formatting**: Use ''mix format'' to maintain consistent code style\n- **Continuous Refactoring**: Regularly improve code structure without changing behavior\n- **Comments**: Write comments only when necessary. Describe why, not what it does.\n\n## Performance Considerations\n\n- **Avoid N+1 Queries**: Use Ecto''s preloading and joins\n- **Pagination**: Paginate large result sets\n- **Background Jobs**: Use Oban for background processing\n- **Measure First**: Profile before optimizing\n- **Caching**: Apply strategic caching where appropriate\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-03T14:39:27.927Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing structured React development guidelines based on Elixir and Phoenix best practices","zh":"非常适合需要基于 Elixir 和 Phoenix 最佳实践的结构化 React 开发指南的前端智能体","ja":"Elixir と Phoenix のベストプラクティスに基づいた構造化された React 開発ガイドラインを必要とするフロントエンドエージェントに最適です","ko":"Elixir와 Phoenix의 모범 사례를 기반으로 한 구조화된 React 개발 가이드라인이 필요한 프론트엔드 에이전트에 완벽합니다","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Frontend que necesitan directrices de desarrollo estructuradas de React basadas en las mejores prácticas de Elixir y Phoenix","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Frontend ayant besoin de lignes directrices de développement React structurées basées sur les meilleures pratiques d''Elixir et Phoenix","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agents, die strukturierte React-Entwicklungsrichtlinien basierend auf den Best Practices von Elixir und Phoenix benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que necessitam de diretrizes estruturadas de desenvolvimento em React baseadas nas melhores práticas de Elixir e Phoenix","ru":"Идеально подходит для Frontend-агентов, которым требуются структурированные руководства по разработке на React, основанные на лучших практиках Elixir и Phoenix","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الواجهة الأمامية الذين يحتاجون إلى إرشادات تطوير مهيكلة لـ React تستند إلى أفضل الممارسات في Elixir و Phoenix"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to organize code around business domains using Domain-Driven Design, implement Functional Core, Imperative Shell architecture, and prefer Explicit Over Implicit coding principles, all while leveraging the latest versions of packages and libraries, including Phoenix","zh":"使智能体能够使用领域驱动设计围绕业务领域组织代码，实现功能核心、命令式外壳架构，并倾向于显式优于隐式的编码原则，同时利用包括 Phoenix 在内的最新版本的包和库","ja":"ドメイン駆動設計を使用してビジネスドメインごとにコードを整理し、Functional Core、Imperative Shell アーキテクチャを実装し、明示的を暗黙的よりも優先するコーディング原則を好み、Phoenix を含むパッケージとライブラリの最新バージョンを活用するようにエージェントを支援します","ko":"에이전트가 도메인 주도 설계를 사용하여 비즈니스 도메인을 중심으로 코드를 구성하고, Functional Core, Imperative Shell 아키텍처를 구현하며, 명시적이 암시적보다 우선하는 코딩 원칙을 선호하도록 하며, Phoenix를 포함한 패키지 및 라이브러리의 최신 버전을 활용할 수 있게 합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a organizar el código alrededor de dominios empresariales utilizando Domain-Driven Design, implementar arquitectura de Functional Core, Imperative Shell y preferir principios de codificación Explicit Over Implicit, todo mientras aprovecha las versiones más recientes de paquetes y bibliotecas, incluyendo Phoenix","fr":"Permet aux agents d''organiser le code autour de domaines commerciaux en utilisant Domain-Driven Design, de mettre en œuvre une architecture de Functional Core, Imperative Shell et de préférer des principes de codage Explicit Over Implicit, le tout en exploitant les dernières versions de packages et de bibliothèques, y compris Phoenix","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Code um Geschäftsbereiche herum zu organisieren, indem sie Domain-Driven Design verwenden, eine Functional Core, Imperative Shell-Architektur implementieren und Explizit-über-Implicit-Codierungsprinzipien bevorzugen, alles bei Nutzung der neuesten Versionen von Paketen und Bibliotheken, einschließlich Phoenix","pt":"Capacita os agentes a organizar o código em torno de domínios de negócio usando Domain-Driven Design, implementar a arquitetura Functional Core, Imperative Shell e preferir os princípios de codificação Explicit Over Implicit, tudo isso aproveitando as versões mais recentes de pacotes e bibliotecas, incluindo Phoenix","ru":"Позволяет агентам организовывать код вокруг бизнес-доменов, используя Domain-Driven Design, внедрять архитектуру Functional Core, Imperative Shell и отдавать предпочтение принципам кодирования Explicit Over Implicit, все это с использованием последних версий пакетов и библиотек, включая Phoenix","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من تنظيم الكود حول المجالات التجارية باستخدام Domain-Driven Design، وتنفيذ بنية Functional Core، Imperative Shell، وتفضيل مبادئ الترميز الصريح على الضمني، كل ذلك مع الاستفادة من أحدث إصدارات الحزم والمكتبات، بما في ذلك Phoenix"},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing Domain-Driven Design in React applications","Building systems using Composition Over Inheritance principles","Enforcing Explicit Over Implicit coding standards for clarity"],"zh":["在 React 应用程序中实施领域驱动设计","使用组合优于继承原则构建系统","为清晰度而强制执行显式优于隐式的编码标准"],"ja":["React アプリケーションでのドメイン駆動設計の実装","コンポジション over 継承の原則を使用したシステムの構築","明確性のための明示的を暗黙的よりも優先するコーディング標準の強制"],"ko":["React 애플리케이션에서 도메인 주도 설계 구현","상속보다는 구성 원칙을 사용하여 시스템 구축","명확성을 위한 명시적이 암시적보다 우선하는 코딩 표준 적용"],"es":["Implementar Domain-Driven Design en aplicaciones React","Construir sistemas utilizando principios de Composition Over Inheritance","Hacer cumplir los estándares de codificación Explicit Over Implicit para la claridad"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre Domain-Driven Design dans les applications React","Construire des systèmes en utilisant des principes de Composition Over Inheritance","Faire respecter les normes de codage Explicit Over Implicit pour la clarté"],"de":["Domain-Driven Design in React-Anwendungen implementieren","Systeme mithilfe von Composition-Over-Inheritance-Prinzipien aufbauen","Explizit-über-Implicit-Codierungsstandards für Klarheit durchsetzen"],"pt":["Implementação de Domain-Driven Design em aplicações React","Construção de sistemas usando os princípios de Composition Over Inheritance","Imposição de padrões de codificação Explicit Over Implicit para maior clareza"],"ru":["Внедрение Domain-Driven Design в приложениях React","Построение систем с использованием принципов Composition Over Inheritance","Применение стандартов кодирования Explicit Over Implicit для ясности"],"ar":["تنفيذ Domain-Driven Design في تطبيقات React","بناء أنظمة باستخدام مبادئ التركيب على الميراث Composition Over Inheritance","فرض معايير الترميز الصريح على الضمني Explicit Over Implicit من أجل الوضوح"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Elixir and Phoenix coding philosophy","Limited to React-based projects","Dependent on latest package and library versions"],"zh":["需要理解 Elixir 和 Phoenix 的编码理念","仅限于基于 React 的项目","依赖于最新的包和库版本"],"ja":["Elixir と Phoenix のコーディング哲学の理解が必要","React ベースのプロジェクトに限定される","最新のパッケージとライブラリのバージョンに依存"],"ko":["Elixir 및 Phoenix 코딩 철학에 대한 이해 필요","React 기반 프로젝트로 제한됨","최신 패키지 및 라이브러리 버전에 의존"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de la filosofía de codificación de Elixir y Phoenix","Limitado a proyectos basados en React","Dependiente de las versiones más recientes de paquetes y bibliotecas"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension de la philosophie de codage d''Elixir et Phoenix","Limité aux projets basés sur React","Dépendant des dernières versions de packages et de bibliothèques"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis für die Kodierungsphilosophie von Elixir und Phoenix","Begrenzt auf React-basierte Projekte","Abhängig von den neuesten Versionen von Paketen und Bibliotheken"],"pt":["Requer compreensão da filosofia de codificação de Elixir e Phoenix","Limitado a projetos baseados em React","Dependente das versões mais recentes de pacotes e bibliotecas"],"ru":["Требует понимания философии программирования на Elixir и Phoenix","Ограничено проектами на основе React","Зависит от последних версий пакетов и библиотек"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم فلسفة الترميز في Elixir و Phoenix","يقتصر على المشاريع القائمة على React","يعتمد على أحدث إصدارات الحزم والمكتبات"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"d067477f8f8bcfd714138814f81bffc78818ff1710c59e81ddaeeb21ca38e55e","qualityScore":27}');
